    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0769" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79693/9–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-09-14T17:00:00+09:00">September 14,
                            1946—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 15—1:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1485. General Marshall approved Embassy’s telegram 1477, September 13, 1 p.m.,
                    which was despatched before Department’s telegram <pb facs="0770" n="760"
                        xml:id="pg760"/> 736, September 10, 7 p.m., was decoded. In these
                    circumstances, is Department content to await results of action already
                    taken?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
